components.responsibility:
InlineData rows over ChooseTestsRoot:
- TEMP under %SystemRoot% in any letter case is redirected;
- the user's own TEMP is unchanged;
- a TEMP that only shares the name prefix (C:\WindowsTemp, C:\Windows.old\Temp) is unchanged;
- a redirect target that is itself under %SystemRoot% throws the named refusal.

key_decisions.rationale:
Measured in every layer:
- 20/23 vs 23/23 and 689/692 vs 692/692, depending only on TEMP;
- fsutil reports ENABLED in both locations;
- the real Scanner gives (7,7) with 3 of 7 folders moved, 5 of 5 trees;
- parent-first back-dating reset 6 of 8 folders, deepest-first reset 0.

key_decisions.decision:
Under a machine TEMP, TempTree roots fixtures in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Temp\fsa-tests:
- through a pure ChooseTestsRoot;
- with a named refusal if that target is also under %SystemRoot%;
- with the NTFS and compression refusals unchanged.
The engine-side HKCU TEMP fix is not built here.

key_decisions.rationale:
The workaround rule covers the app stepping around an outside defect by skipping, refusing, rerouting or retrying. This slice does none of that:
- the scan does exactly what it did;
- the correction fixes this project's own false count;
- the redirect lives in test fixtures, not in the app.

An off switch would only bring the false number back, and nobody sees that number (Q-103, Q-159). If file-age features ever surface last access, the luafv limit becomes a notice question for that slice.

proposals.note:
The only proposal. Taken almost whole. Changes:
- the location test reuses Scanner's existing IsAtOrUnder;
- the parent is derived with string operations in the counted form;
- ChooseTestsRoot is made pure, with its own InlineData Facts;
- the Windows-folder Facts get a root-spelling Theory, an outside-%SystemRoot% case and a tree-gone assertion.
Its over_engineering_flag was honoured: nothing it listed as over-built is built.

taste_disagreements:
Where the TEMP problem is fixed:
- TempTree redirect (chosen; works whatever launches the suite);
- the engine launching with the HKCU TEMP (spike 5 go; outside this repo);
- TempTree refusing a %SystemRoot% TEMP outright (keeps the suite red under the engine).
